"""ycash-bootstrap: restore a checkpoint bundle into an empty datadir (testnet plan §4.4).

    ycash-bootstrap --network testnet-yb-fast --datadir DIR [--source URL|DIR] [--reset] [--verify-full]
    ycash-bootstrap --network regtest --datadir DIR --pack OUT --last-height N   # make a regtest bundle

Two layers (§4.0). The **prefix** (the default): Zcash testnet blocks 0..510,247 in the frozen
format `ycash-prefix/1` (ycash-infra `bundles/prefix/FORMAT.md`), shared by the three testnets
because it carries no network magic. The **state bundle** (`--state --source DIR|URL`): a ycash6
datadir at a height H_B above the fork in the format `ycash-state/1` (ycash-infra
`bundles/state/FORMAT.md`), checked against its verifiers' statements (below the prefix steps).

Restoring, in order, refusing at the first failure:
  1. the target network's subdirectory (`testnet-yb-fast`, ...) must hold no chain yet; `--reset`
     first moves an existing wallet.dat aside and removes that subdirectory (testnet resets, T-7);
  2. `SHA256SUMS` is fetched; its own sha256 must equal the value this release pins for the
     network (the profile's `prefix.sha256sums_sha256`); a `SHA256SUMS.minisig` beside it must
     verify with the owner's key (keys/ycash-release.pub; optional until the bundle is signed,
     mandatory with `--require-signature`);
  3. `manifest.json` must match its sum and the release: format, network, the chunk rule, the
     last height and hash (= the compiled checkpoint), the compiled earlier checkpoints;
  4. every chunk is downloaded and checked against `SHA256SUMS` and the manifest, then framed for
     `-loadblock` with the network's magic (`<magic> <LE u32 length> <block>`), checking the hash
     chain, the genesis, every manifest hash, the raw size and sha256 on the way;
  5. `ycashd` imports the framed files with `-connect=0 -listen=0 -disablewallet` (so a wallet is
     created, from -mnemonicfile or not, only at the node's first normal start; and `-checkpoints=0` under
     `--verify-full`, which validates every block's scripts instead of trusting the checkpoint);
  6. the node must reach the last height with `getblockhash` equal to the manifest at every listed
     height and to the compiled checkpoint at the last; then it is stopped and the framed files
     are removed. Start the node normally afterwards.

A state bundle: SHA256SUMS (and its signature, as above), the canonical manifest (format, the
profile's network and -testnetprofile, line ycash6, H_B above the fork, the tarball's name and
sum), at least two byte-identical statements that agree with it; the tarball's sha256 and size;
extraction of directories and regular files under `<network>/{blocks,chainstate,vaults,yellowback}`
only (no wallet, no LevelDB LOCK/LOG, no links); then the node starts offline, settles, rolls back
with `invalidateblock H_B+1` when it connected blocks above H_B, must produce the statement's
fields itself (getblockhash, chainwork, gettxoutsetinfo, vault_getinfo, yed_getstatehash), and
`reconsiderblock`s. A failure removes what was extracted.

Nothing in a bundle is executed; file names are checked against the format before they become a
path or a URL. Python standard library only (plus the `minisign` binary when a signature is
present); run it with `python3 -I`.
"""

